TYPES.md §1, §7.2, WIRE.md §4.1 (progen nightly, E3201 "code outside its @codes type"): a member code outside its `@codes` type is E3201 and the member has no code, so `@json(bits)` judges only the members with a code (no E3316 for it); a member with a code that is no power of two is still E3316.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local enum Flag @codes(UInt32) {
  a = 1
  b = 4294967296
  c = 4
}

local enum Bad @codes(UInt32) {
  x = 1
  y = 4294967296
  z = 3
}

local record R {
  flags: [Flag] @json(bits)
  bad: [Bad] @json(bits)
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3201]  a/a.canon:5:7
  4294967296 does not fit UInt32

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:11:7
  4294967296 does not fit UInt32

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:17:20
  @json(bits) needs every code of a.Bad to be a power of two from 1 to 2^62

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
